This crate (`symphonia-codec-ac3`) is a pure-Rust AC-3 (ATSC A/52) and Enhanced AC-3 (ETSI TS 102 366
Annex E) decoder. It is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project
Symphonia (see `LICENSE`).

Specification-derived data
--------------------------

All constant tables in `src/tables.rs` (bit-allocation tables, quantizer tables, window, scale-factor
and band tables, E-AC-3 vector-quantization and gain-adaptive-quantization tables, spectral extension
attenuation table, enhanced coupling amplitude table, default band structures, channel-map locations)
are extracted programmatically from the machine-readable text of ETSI TS 102 366 V1.3.1 / V1.4.1. They
were not typed in by hand.

Algorithms derived from FFmpeg
------------------------------

The decoder follows the structure and the integer-mantissa arithmetic of FFmpeg's `libavcodec/ac3dec.c`,
`eac3dec.c`, `ac3dec_float.c` and `ac3.c` (parsing order, exponent/mantissa decoding, the spectral
extension and coupling reconstruction, the 64-tap lagged-Fibonacci dither generator and its seed
table, which is generated by the same MD5 based procedure as `av_lfg_init`) so that its output is
numerically comparable to FFmpeg's. FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License,
version 2.1 or later; its copyright notices follow:

